          "message": "ci(velvet): run PlayMode benchmarks one iteration on pull requests and record full-count trends (#1349)\n\n## What & why\n\nThe PlayMode benchmarks (`Velvet.Tests.Performance`) assert nothing about their numbers. They still took about 68% of the required PlayMode run, and the numbers they produced were recorded nowhere.\n\n**One iteration in the required run**\n- `TestUtilities/BenchmarkRun` gives every benchmark one measured iteration and no warmup by default.\n- The editor flag `-velvetBenchmarkFull` restores the counts each benchmark declares.\n- The required run, base-red and the mutation campaign pass no flag. They keep each benchmark's exception coverage at a fraction of the time.\n\n**Paths that only a later iteration reaches**\n- An unmount after a mount, or a mount that rents what an earlier unmount pooled, would go unexercised with one iteration.\n- Such paths now run once more, unconditionally, outside the measured window, in:\n  - the end-to-end mount benchmark;\n  - `Mount_100StyledRows`;\n  - the `Hooks.Use` and route-loader loops.\n\n**Full counts in their own workflow (`.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml`, not required)**\n- It runs on:\n  - every push to `main` that changes the package;\n  - a manual dispatch;\n  - a pull request carrying the `benchmarks` label, at labelling and on every later push.\n- Each run uploads the results XML and writes the medians to the job summary.\n- `scripts/ci/benchmark_results.py` converts Unity Performance Testing's `##performancetestresult2:` lines into the shape `benchmark-action/github-action-benchmark` reads. `scripts/ci/test_benchmark_results.py` holds that converter.\n\n**History**\n- `trend-main` appends each `main` run to the `benchmark-data` branch under `dev/bench`. The branch is created as an orphan on first use.\n- The `Docs` workflow copies that directory into the Pages site, so the chart is published at `/dev/bench/` with the next docs deployment.\n- `trend-pull-request` compares a labelled head with `main`'s latest entry in the job summary.\n- Neither job gates on a number, because CI timings are too noisy for that.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md ▸ Benchmarks owns when the benchmarks run, where the numbers live and how to read them.\n\nThe `benchmarks` label has to exist in the repository. Nothing in the workflow creates it.\n\nRefs #1345\n\n## Cases the base reading cannot redden\n\nThe base reading carries `TestUtilities/BenchmarkRun.cs` along with the tests, so the four `BenchmarkRunTests` cases run this branch's helper on both sides. Each is declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(construction)` with a perturbation. The perturbations are derived from the helper's two-line bodies, not run in an editor:\n\n| Perturbation | Case | Fails because |\n|---|---|---|\n| `IsFull` returns true | no-flag case | asserts `(true, 5, 20)` against `(false, 0, 1)` |\n| `IsFull` returns false | full-flag case | asserts `(false, 0, 1)` against `(true, 5, 20)` |\n| `Warmup` returns its argument | the zero-warmup case | reads 5 against 0 |\n| `Measurements` returns its argument | the one-measurement case | reads 20 against 1 |\n\n## Remaining\n\n- The `benchmarks` label is not created yet.\n- The first `main` entry and the first chart deployment happen only after this merges.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable). Run locally: `scripts/ci` Python tests, and the duplication, assume-gate and stranded-name checks. Unity suites run in CI.\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it. `BenchmarkRunTests` and the converter tests reference surfaces that are new here.\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches: CONTRIBUTING.md (Benchmarks, the workflow table) and AGENTS.md (the benchmark line).\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment: none. This changes CI and tests only; no package behaviour or performance changes.\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria. None were found beyond the Remaining items above.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
