          "message": "test(velvet): record panel fixture window cost per case in CI (#1352)\n\n## What & why\n\nEach `PanelTestBase` fixture creates, shows and closes an `EditorWindow` per case. Whether sharing one window per fixture would pay off depends on a cost nobody has measured, so this change measures it in CI. That is step 1 of #1346.\n\n**What it records**\n- `PanelTestBase` now times four phases per case with a `Stopwatch`:\n  - `create_show`: `CreateInstance` + `Show`\n  - `layout`: each `EditorPanelTestHelpers.ForcePanelUpdate`\n  - `teardown`: `Close` + `DestroyImmediate`\n  - `case`: the whole span from the base `SetUp` to the end of the base `TearDown`\n- `TestUtilities/PanelPhaseTimings` buffers the rows in memory and appends them once per fixture, at its `[OneTimeTearDown]`.\n- The rows go to `panel-phase-timings.csv` in the directory of the `-testResults` file, which is the EditMode results directory CI already uploads.\n- Recording never throws into a case and logs nothing.\n- With no `-testResults`, nothing is written.\n\n**How it is reported**\n- `scripts/ci/panel_phase_timings.py` summarises the CSV: totals and means per phase, the window cost as a share of the panel cases and of the suite, and the fixtures with the highest window cost. The output goes to the log and the job summary.\n- A missing CSV, or a missing results XML, is reported as unknown with a warning, never as a number.\n- test.yml runs the summariser after the EditMode upload, and runs its unittests beside the other `scripts/ci` tests.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md ▸ Panel fixture timing says what is and is not measured.\n\nRefs #1346\n\n## Remaining\n\n- Step 2 of #1346 is still open: if window creation dominates, reuse one window per fixture. That is decided from the first CI run's CSV.\n- The NUnit per-case duration convention (whether it includes setup and teardown) is still to be confirmed from that same run's XML.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable): the `scripts/ci` tests, the generator suite, and the duplication, assume-gate and stranded-name checks, plus `--refusals` and `base_red_check --plan` and its own suite. The Unity suites run in CI.\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it. The C# cases are declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(construction)`, each naming its cut; those cuts are traced, not run. The Python cases depend on surfaces only this branch adds.\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment: none, since this is test and contributor tooling only.\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria. They stay on #1346.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
