          "distinct": true,
          "id": "93637fdcf7f57282eb1f0d517a27dad427f180ca",
          "message": "fix(velvet): remove unread query entries when their gcTime passes (#1362)\n\n## What & why\n\nA `QueryClient` entry that no query reads was removed only when a later client call swept it: a subscribe, `InvalidateQueries` or `SetQueryData`. Until one of those came, an idle application kept every inactive entry and its data. TanStack Query v5 instead removes an unread query when its `gcTime` runs out, using the timer that `Removable.scheduleGc` sets.\n\n**The change:**\n- When an entry that can expire goes inactive, `MarkInactive` starts one collection loop for the client. The loop polls the client's clock once a frame and removes each entry whose `GcTime` has passed. Removal therefore lands on the first frame whose clock reading is at or past the deadline.\n- The loop skips walking the inactive list until the earliest deadline it knows of. It ends as soon as no entry that can expire is left: none at all, or only `TimeSpan.MaxValue` entries.\n- A reader arriving before the deadline keeps the entry. The countdown starts over when its last reader leaves.\n- The loop holds the client only through a `WeakReference`, so a client the application drops is not kept alive by its own loop.\n- The time source is the existing `QueryClientOptions.Clock` seam, the same one `StaleTime`, `RefetchInterval` and the retry wait already read.\n\n**v5 parity.** These rules were checked against `@tanstack/query-core@5.62.0` (`removable.ts`, `query.ts`, `queryCache.ts`):\n- `isValidTimeout` sets no timer for `Infinity`. Here, `TimeSpan.MaxValue` is never collected.\n- `gcTime` 0 removes the entry on the next tick. Here, `Zero` removes it on the next frame.\n- `addObserver` clears the timer and `removeObserver` reschedules it.\n- `updateGcTime` keeps the largest `gcTime` any query asked for.\n- `optionalRemove` removes only an idle query. An entry with a request in flight is kept until a whole `GcTime` after the request settles.\n\n**Departure from the issue's acceptance list.** The issue says the timer \"cancels its in-flight request\". v5 does not do that, as explained in the correction comment on the issue, so this PR keeps the entry instead.\n\n**Docs.** The \"Garbage collection runs no timer\" deviation is removed from `react-migration.md`, and a paragraph describing the collection replaces it. The `QueryClient` remarks and `QueryClientOptions.GcTime` XML docs are updated to match.\n\n**Tests.** `QueryClientGcTimerTests` contains 16 cases. They advance a hand clock and observe the loop through the number of clock reads per frame, without reading private state. The only reflection is on `_entries`, which main also has. They cover:\n- removal at the deadline, and not one tick before it;\n- `Zero` and `MaxValue`;\n- a reader returning before the deadline;\n- a request in flight;\n- one loop per client;\n- the loop ending, and restarting, once nothing can expire, including after a lazy sweep, `Clear`, or a reader returning;\n- a clock that throws.\n\nThe cases that assert polling stops are declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`, because main never polls. Each is paired with a case that is red on main.\n\nCloses #1320\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
