          "id": "01acf907fc26b964b38b671d6b56e6a5eb52ff58",
          "message": "fix(velvet): resolve overlapping rounded-* by Tailwind's property order (#1366)\n\n## What & why\n\nTwo `rounded-*` utilities that write different properties but share a corner were settled by class order, or by the order of the bundled stylesheet. In `rounded-t-[2px] rounded-r-[8px]` the top-right corner was whichever came last. Tailwind v4 instead sorts its utilities by property, and the one it emits later holds the shared corner whichever is written first. Both orders of that pair give the top-right corner 8px in Tailwind.\n\n**The change:**\n- `StyleRuleOrder.CompareUtilities` orders two utilities as Tailwind emits them, from the existing property-order sort key.\n- `StyleSpacingPrecedence` reads the overlapping radius tokens of one `className` and writes the winner of each shared corner inline. A stylesheet class that takes part in such a pair therefore leaves the element's class list.\n- Six logical-radius `ArbitraryProperty` members (`rounded-s-*`, `rounded-e-*`, `rounded-ss-*`, `rounded-se-*`, `rounded-es-*`, `rounded-ee-*`) let the logical forms take part, for a bracket value and for a scale step alike.\n- `_borders.uss` declares the radius rules in Tailwind's order, so two classes on one element no longer depend on the order of the sheet. `StyleUtilityProperties.g.cs` and `_radius_declared.uss` are regenerated from it.\n- A `V.Motion` pose keeps the corners it writes. A base radius it partly overlaps is cut down to the corners the pose leaves.\n- `StyleShadowClass.TryResolveCornerRadius` ranks the radius tokens the same way, so a shadow or ring follows the box's corner radius.\n\n**Out of scope:** border widths and the ordering of two utilities that write the same property belong to #1279 and #1322.\n\n**Docs and changelog.** `styling-arbitrary-lengths.md` describes the resolution. Fragments are added under `unreleased` and `breaking`: a corner that used to follow the class order or the sheet order now follows Tailwind's property order.\n\n**Tests.** `RadiusPrecedenceTests` covers the following, with the utility Tailwind emits later written both first and last, and with `!` importance and a `hover:` variant:\n- the shorthand against a side or a corner;\n- a side against a corner;\n- a side against a side;\n- the logical forms against the physical ones;\n- the radius utilities sorted by their cascade rank;\n- a stylesheet radius class written inline beside a bracket one it overlaps;\n- the Motion pose cut;\n- the shadow radius.\n\n`ArbitraryValueTests` and `StyleArbitraryLonghandTableTests` follow the new property members.\n\nCloses #1341\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
