          "distinct": true,
          "id": "71268635606978c021839fa52c05731e9faa0f51",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: render a Suspense-hidden primary as an attempt that commits nothing (#1368)\n\n## What & why\n\nA `V.Suspense` that shows its fallback over children it had already shown can still render those children on an update. Each such render promoted the children's hook deps in `FiberBeginWork.CommitSettledHookDeps`, whether or not a commit followed. So an effect whose deps changed and then changed back while the fallback showed ran again at the reveal. `FiberEffects.HoldInsertionEffects` existed only to carry insertion effects across these renders.\n\nReact handles this differently, as checked against `ReactFiberBeginWork.js`. A boundary showing its fallback does attempt its primary again when an update reaches it. That attempt is a work-in-progress render. If it suspends again it is discarded: it queues no effects and promotes no deps, because deps are compared against the last committed render. The correction comment on #1358 explains why the issue's \"React does not render it\" premise overstates this.\n\n**The change:**\n- A re-render of an existing fiber under a Suspense primary that retains its committed children is recorded instead of settled.\n  - `FiberRenderer.SettleHooks` commits the context reads and the callback and memo values right away, as on main.\n  - It records the fiber with its pending insertion and passive lengths.\n- Once `GeneralPathReconciler.ExpandSuspenseInline` knows whether the primary suspended, `ReconcilerContext.ResolveSuspenseRenders` settles each record.\n  - If the primary suspended, the record is discarded: the queued effects are truncated, and the fiber is marked dirty so it renders again at the reveal.\n  - If the primary did not suspend, the record is committed. Effect and blocker deps are promoted, or the record is handed to an enclosing retaining primary.\n- `HoldInsertionEffects` and `ComponentFiber.HeldInsertionEffects` are removed. `HoldWhileHidden` stays, because components first mounted under a fallback still rely on it.\n- One deviation remains, and `react-migration.md` records it. Velvet's attempt also renders the children after the one that suspends, and `UseMemo`/`UseCallback` values computed in a discarded attempt stand. Keeping those values is what keeps strict mode's double render matching main.\n\n**Breaking:** in a primary that had been shown, a component reached by a hidden render renders once more for the reveal. An effect that used to run at the reveal because its deps changed and changed back no longer runs. The details are in the `breaking/` fragment.\n\n**Docs and changelog:** `react-migration.md` (the Suspense paragraph), plus fragments under `unreleased/` and `breaking/`.\n\n**Tests:** `SuspenseHiddenAttemptTests`.\n- Expected red on main:\n  - the insertion, passive and nested-boundary A→B→A cases.\n- `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`:\n  - the render count at the reveal;\n  - a memoized probe;\n  - a reveal followed by a same-deps render;\n  - a render with changed deps that suspended;\n  - a memoized context consumer under a shown boundary, which pins that context subscriptions are not dropped;\n  - strict mode running a memo factory once per render.\n\nCloses #1358\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
