          "distinct": true,
          "id": "72e9ee7f5481e038685f536a7130dfd1e2b480b1",
          "message": "fix(velvet)!: attach host refs in the layout walk, between the layout effects, as React commits them (#1376)\n\n## What & why\n\nA commit attached every host `refCallback:` before its first layout effect. React does it differently. `commitLayoutEffects` (`ReactFiberCommitWork.js`) walks the finished tree once and, on each fiber's completion, runs that fiber's work:\n- a host component's ref attach;\n- a function component's layout effects.\n\nSo an element's ref attaches after everything inside it, and after the layout effects of the components below it. A component's layout effects run after the refs of the elements it rendered. On mount, a `useLayoutEffect` cannot see an ancestor element's ref or a later sibling's.\n\n**The change:**\n- **Refs attach in the layout walk.** The layout phase walks the committed tree in React's completion order and attaches each host ref as it reaches the element, between the layout effects.\n  - `FiberRefPlacement` records where each pending attach sits relative to the layout effects of its pass.\n  - `FiberEffects` runs the attaches and effects interleaved.\n- **Detach before cleanup.** Layout cleanups run after the refs they replace detach, and before the new refs attach. This matches React's mutation-then-layout order.\n- **Batched drains.** A batched drain attaches the refs of every component it re-rendered at the drain's end, interleaved with the drain's layout effects.\n- **Portals.** A `V.Portal`'s element refs attach where the portal sits among its neighbours.\n- **Nested owed-settle flush.** A nested owed-settle flush does not take the enclosing commit's refs.\n- **Enter completions.** An enter completion that is owed while a ref setup is still pending waits for the layout commit. Exit completions keep running from the passive-effect flush.\n\n**Breaking:** a `Hooks.UseLayoutEffect` on mount no longer finds an ancestor's ref, or a later sibling's, set. It still finds its own component's refs, its descendants' and its earlier siblings'. The `breaking/` fragment has the full list.\n\n**Docs and changelog:**\n- `react-migration.md` and `portals.md` describe the commit order.\n- A `breaking/` fragment is added.\n- The `fix-1122-portals-parity` fragment's sentence on ref-identity cleanup is corrected to the new timing.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `RefLayoutInterleaveTests` pins the order of ref attaches against layout effects for:\n  - a parent and its child;\n  - siblings;\n  - a portal;\n  - a batched drain;\n  - layout cleanups;\n  - the nested owed-settle flush;\n  - `VirtualList` rows rendered from a drain or a scroll;\n  - a `V.Motion` whose enter plays nothing.\n- Cases the base already answers carry `GREEN_ON_BASE` declarations.\n\nCloses #1288\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
