          "id": "5cf3b44364b3cb66473e383f07bcd8e2609b3bf2",
          "message": "test(velvet): prune spacing-step and motion-default cases other cases already cover (#1391)\n\n## What & why\n\nThis removes eight test cases whose behaviour and mutant kills other cases already cover.\n\n- **`SpacingStepTests`.**\n  - Removes seven `TryGetSpacingPx` rows:\n    - the positive rows `17.75`, `100` and `1.5`;\n    - the decline rows `00`, `4.0`, `4.` and `0.125`.\n  - The kept rows still reach each branch of `StyleSpacingMultiplier.TryParse`:\n    - `13` for the whole-number branch;\n    - `4.5`, `0.25` and `0.75` for the three fraction branches;\n    - `05` for the leading-zero branch;\n    - `4.50` and `4.1` for `QuartersOf == 0`.\n- **`AnimatePresenceTests`.** `Given_DefaultMotion_..._Then_ElementTypeIsVisualElement` is removed. Its body is byte-identical to `Given_NoElementType_When_MotionBuilt_Then_DefaultsToVisualElement`, which stays.\n\n**Kill-set proof.** A `kill-set.yml` run on head `ed549bc5` against base `20d76a71` (run 38954586329) covered the members these rows reach:\n- `StyleSpacingMultiplier.cs`, whole;\n- `StyleArbitraryValueResolver.cs` `TryParseWhole`;\n- `StyleArbitraryValueResolver.cs` `TryParseSpacingStep`.\n\nIt reports `11 mutant(s); killed on the base: 9, lost on the head: 0`. The duplicate `AnimatePresenceTests` body cannot kill a mutant the kept one does not.\n\n**Case counts:** `SpacingStepTests` goes from 240 to 233, and `AnimatePresenceTests` from 67 to 66.\n\n**No user-facing change.** Test-only, so no CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` impact.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
