          "id": "363b12467f5c9703b2964ad1961468b72e35a5a0",
          "message": "test(velvet): pin where an absolute element with no inset sits (#1396)\n\n## What & why\n\nThe issue asked whether an absolutely positioned element with all insets `auto` sits at its CSS static position. Measurement shows UI Toolkit already matches css-flexbox for flex containers: such a child sits as the flex container's sole flex item, so a preceding sibling does not move it. The issue's expected y=30 does not hold in a browser either. No runtime change is needed.\n\n**The change:**\n- Panel tests pin the column and row cases, with and without padding, one-axis insets, and `top-auto left-auto`.\n- `react-migration.md` states the position for `flex` and `flex-col` containers and makes no claim for `grid`.\n\n**Changelog:** an unreleased fragment for the documented behaviour.\n\nCloses #1275\n\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
