          "id": "e76208dd49f07d2e36d64ccaaa23219180d2d8d3",
          "message": "fix(velvet): transition a swap between two bracketed width classes (#1394)\n\n## What & why\n\nSwapping one bracketed width class for another, such as `w-[300px]` to `w-[10px]`, landed without its transition. Removing the outgoing class re-resolved the layer and wrote the new width before the transition could see the change.\n\n**The change:** `RemoveOutgoingClass` withdraws the outgoing arbitrary layer without resolving it, through `StyleArbitraryValueResolver.Withdraw`. The existing reapply then writes the incoming value, so the transition runs from the old width.\n\n**Docs:** a paragraph in `styling-arbitrary-lengths.md`. **Changelog:** an unreleased fragment.\n\n**Tests:** `ArbitraryWidthSwapTransitionTests` covers px and `vw`, `!` variants, a wider swap, ten or more classes, and swapping to nothing.\n\nCloses #1311\n\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
