          "id": "3618d54004f618acf2023c0a5da2e3986b5e40a6",
          "message": "fix(velvet): scope the hsl() saturation clamp to Chromium's colour longhands (#1393)\n\n## What & why\n\nAn `hsl()` saturation outside 0–100% was clamped the same way everywhere, which differs from Chromium. Chromium clamps saturation only when its fast path parses a plain `hsl()` on a colour longhand. Huge finite components and hues read as non-finite.\n\n**The change:**\n- **Saturation clamp:** applies only to a plain `hsl()`/`hsla()` on colour longhands, as Chromium's fast path does. A space-syntax lightness is floored at 0.\n- **Overflowing numbers:** clamp to `float.MaxValue` instead of reading as infinite, so a huge hue resolves the way an equivalent finite hue does.\n- **`lab()`, `lch()`, `oklab()` and `oklch()`:** Velvet does not read these, so they stay declined whatever their magnitude. `styling-colors.md` now says so, and a case pins it. Implementing them belongs to #1282.\n\n**Docs:** `styling-colors.md`. **Changelog:** an unreleased fragment.\n\n**Tests:** `CssColorHslScopeTests`.\n\nCloses #1314\n\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
