          "message": "feat(velvet)!: queue UseState and UseReducer updates by lane, as React does (#1392)\n\n## What & why\n\n`UseState` and `UseReducer` wrote a setter's result into the hook slot at once. As a result, an urgent render that ran before a transition committed already showed the transition's write. Likewise, an ancestor's Normal pass could commit that write and clear `isPending`.\n\nReact keeps a per-hook update queue instead (`ReactFiberHooks.js`, `updateReducerImpl` / `dispatchSetState`). Each update carries a lane, and a render processes only the updates its lanes include. A skipped update is rebased, so a later render replays it in order over the base state.\n\n**The change:**\n- **Lane-tagged updates.** `HookUpdateQueueSlot` gives `UseState` and `UseReducer` one shared queue.\n  - A Transition update is skipped by any non-Transition render.\n  - Urgent and Normal updates render together, as React's `SyncUpdateLanes` do (`ReactFiberLane.js:55-56,179-183`).\n  - A skip keeps the base state from the first skipped update and re-requests the Transition lane.\n- **Eager state as React computes it.**\n  - `UseState` computes at the call only while nothing is queued. An equal result still queues an unscheduled update, as `enqueueConcurrentHookUpdateAndEagerlyBailout` does.\n  - `UseReducer` never computes at the call (`dispatchReducerAction`). The render's own reducer decides the state.\n  - A replayed update that ran at the call reuses its result (`ReactFiberHooks.js:1537`). A lazy update runs at the render.\n- **Render lane.**\n  - `FiberWorkLoop.RenderLane` is set by each flush and by `ContinueReconcile`, and is restored after both.\n  - Outside a flush it is Normal, so an async-resource retry does not fold in a transition's writes.\n- **Commit with the render.**\n  - State commits with the render's settled effects.\n  - A render that Suspense discards leaves its updates queued.\n- **Pooled-node safety.** The recycle sweep marks every node the queue can still emit:\n  - committed and base state;\n  - payloads and eager results of pending and base-queue updates;\n  - staged state.\n- **Disposal.** A setter on a disposed component stays a no-op.\n\n**Breaking:**\n- Until the Transition render commits, a transition's write is invisible to urgent and Normal renders, including an ancestor's pass. Such a pass no longer commits it or clears `isPending`.\n- A functional updater queued behind another update runs at the render.\n- A reducer dispatch always renders.\n\nThe `breaking/` fragment has the list.\n\n**Docs:** `react-migration.md` (Local State, `useTransition`, and when Transition-lane work renders), the `Documentation~/README.md` index row, and the `UseState` / `StateUpdater` XML docs.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `HookUpdateQueueTests`: rebase, lane grouping, eager and lazy replay, reducer swap, render-phase writes, disposal, repeated equal writes, render-lane restore.\n- `UseTransitionTests`: subsumption by Normal and Transition passes, and a deferred-value reader under a store write.\n- `RenderedTreePropsRecycleTests`: one case per marked root.\n- Time-sliced resume probes.\n\nEach case asserts one fact.\n\nRefs #1112 (H13). The issue's other items stay open.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
