          "message": "feat(velvet): hold Assets and the package to the same .meta pairing (#1398)\n\n## What & why\n\nTwo `.meta` files for the package's tests had been committed missing, and nothing noticed. `scripts/unity/asset_meta_check.py` now refuses, over what git tracks under `Assets` and `Packages/com.velvet.core`, an asset or directory committed without its `.meta` and a `.meta` committed without its asset. The two missing metas are added, and `Test ▸ test-quality` runs the check and its test suite.\n\nPaths Unity does not import are out of scope, as is a `.meta` naming one: a component starting with `.`, ending with `~` or named `cvs`, and a file ending `.tmp`. Each root itself carries no `.meta`.\n\nThe tests cover a missing file or directory meta, an orphaned file or directory meta, an untracked meta, both roots, paths outside them, the dot, tilde, `cvs` and `.tmp` exclusions, and near-misses (`cvsx`, `a.tmp.cs`) that stay in scope. Each \"nothing is reported\" case asserts one fact, missing or orphaned.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally: `scripts/test_quality/run_suite.py scripts/unity/test_asset_meta_check.py`, 22 tests, all OK; `python3 scripts/unity/asset_meta_check.py` exits 0 on this tree. No Unity suites were run.\n- [x] The `cvs` and `.tmp` tests were verified red with those two rules removed (4 failures) and green with them.\n- [x] No doc impact beyond the `CONTRIBUTING.md` line naming the check.\n- [x] No CHANGELOG fragment: contributor tooling plus metadata files, no package behaviour.\n- [x] No known gaps deferred.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
