          "message": "feat(velvet)!: render isPending true as a transition starts, and hold a parked pass's passive effects until it commits (#1403)\n\n## What & why\n\nRefs #1112 (H2, H20)\n\n**isPending renders at once (H2).** Calling the starter `Hooks.UseTransition` returns now asks for an Urgent-lane\nrender of the declaring component as the call hands control back with the flag still lit. That render shows\n`isPending` true and the state from before the callback's writes, which stay on the Transition lane; the render\nthat commits them follows. React does the same through the sync-lane optimistic update `startTransition`\ndispatches before it runs the callback (`ReactFiberHooks.js`: `startTransition`, `dispatchOptimisticSetState`).\nVelvet used to render nothing purely because the flag turned true.\n\n- Asked only for a flag still lit at that point: a synchronous callback that queued nothing and left no joined\n  call open has settled by then and asks for none, and a call that joins an open transition asks for none of its\n  own. An `async` action asks when it returned a pending task or queued work.\n- The render commits with the handler's own flush inside a discrete event, and for a write that lands on another\n  component than the one declaring the transition.\n- Two things stay as deviations, now stated where the old deviation text stood: a no-op callback renders neither\n  the true nor the false render React gives it, and the render that commits the writes still reads the flag lit,\n  with a follow-up render reading it cleared.\n\n**Passive effects wait for the pass (H20).** The passive drain now holds a fiber whose layout entry waits on the\ndeferred stack under a pass with pending work, so the passive effects of a component a parked time-sliced pass\nrendered, mounted or re-rendered, no longer run between slices. The layout commit that takes the entry stages\nthem again and arms the drain. React runs passive effects only from the phase a commit sets\n(`ReactFiberWorkLoop.js`: `flushPassiveEffects`).\n\n**Tests.** The new cases for H2 are red on the base (no render of the pending state exists there) and the ones for\nH20 are red on the base for the hold. The release side of each is declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`.\nExisting cases that flush a transition now drain the pending render's lane first; those that stay green on the base\nare declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(refactor)`, and those whose counts changed (`4` renders where `3` was) are red on it.\nThe mutation campaign over this change lists 15 mutants, each with a killing case.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity runs are CI's\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — by `Test ▸ base-red`\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — `react-migration.md` (`useTransition` and `useEffect` rows)\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added: `Changelog~/breaking/claude-issue-1112-h2-h20.md`\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria — none beyond the two deviations above\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
